---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { upstreamInfo } from '../lib/content';
const up = upstreamInfo();
---
<Base title="Credits" nav={false}>
  <div class="content-wrap prose">
    <h1>Credits and sources</h1>
    <p>The Primary Care Practice Resource is RoPro's redesigned, interactive site for nurse practitioners, physicians (MD and DO) and students, built on the <a href="https://www.nppr.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NP Practice Resource (NPPR.ca)</a>, created by Joe Grafe and contributors.</p>
    <h2>Content licence</h2>
    <p>The page text comes from the <code>docs/</code> folder of <a href={up.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">joegrafe/np-practice-resource</a> and is used under the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence</a>. Attribution: <a href="https://www.nppr.ca">NPPR.ca</a>. Changes made here: the content is shown in a new layout with new navigation, a dashboard and a research sidebar; the lists and links themselves are unchanged.</p>
    <p>Pages marked "Added here" are not on NPPR.ca. They were written for this site in NPPR's page format, mostly from links in NPPR's source registry and approach lists, including the <a href="https://blackbook.ucalgary.ca/schemes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Calgary Blackbook</a> diagnostic schemes. NPPR.ca has not reviewed them.</p>
    <p>Linked guidelines, PDFs, logos and tools belong to their publishers and are not covered by that licence. This site doesn't host or copy them.</p>
    {up.sha && <p>Content version: <code>{up.sha.slice(0, 7)}</code>, synced {new Date(up.syncedAt).toLocaleString('en-CA')}.</p>}
    <h2>Research sidebar</h2>
    <p>The sidebar on each topic page searches public databases from your browser: <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed</a> (NCBI E-utilities), <a href="https://europepmc.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Europe PMC</a> (free full text and NCBI Bookshelf chapters) and <a href="https://www.wikipedia.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia</a>. Results are not reviewed by NPPR and are not clinical advice.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
